---
layout: layouts/base.njk
schemaType: ProfilePage
title: "About"
metaTitle: "About Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko — AI in Agriculture Speaker, Trainer and Founder"
description: "The story, work and recognition of Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko: founder of MooMore, co-founder of Petiole, LinkedIn Top Voice and Innovate UK Women in Innovation Award 2025/26 winner."
permalink: "/about/"
ogType: "profile"
---
{% from "partials/photo.njk" import photo %}
{% set wiw = facts.award.wiw %}

<section class="bio-page">
  <div class="bio-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko</h1>
    <p class="lead">{{ bios.firstPerson }}</p>
  </div>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <h2>What I do now</h2>

    <div class="bio-card featured">
      <p>
        <strong>Speaking.</strong> I give keynotes, panels and guest lectures on AI in agriculture for agrifood
        conferences, industry meetings and universities, in person or online:
        <a class="inline-link" href="/speaking/">topics and formats</a>.
      </p>

      {{ photo(photos.bridgeAiTalk, sizes="(max-width: 420px) 100vw, 380px", class="page-figure--portrait") }}

      <p>
        <strong>Training.</strong> I train agrifood teams in practical AI literacy, from a short workshop to a
        multi-week course — formats and topics are on <a class="inline-link" href="{{ facts.links.training }}">team training</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Writing and coverage.</strong> I write the {{ facts.newsletter.name }}, host a
        <a class="inline-link" href="{{ facts.live.url }}">{{ facts.live.name | lcfirst }}</a> ↗, publish explainers on
        <a class="inline-link" href="{{ site.social.youtube }}">YouTube</a> ↗ and write the {{ bookSeries }}
        <a class="inline-link" href="/books/">book series</a>. I also report from the sector's main shows:
        <a class="inline-link" href="/insights/">Insights</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="/coverage/">events I've covered</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <h2>What I build</h2>

    <div class="bio-card featured">
      <p>
        I bring nearly 10 years of practical experience in applying digital technologies in agriculture, with a primary
        focus on computer vision and deep learning for plant phenotyping and food quality assurance.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am co-founder and CEO of Petiole, a UK-based SME developing practical AI tools for agriculture and plant
        science. The global platform Petiole Pro, developed by my team, was named a finalist in the GIST Tech-I 2015
        competition in the USA, shortlisted for the UK FPC Fresh Awards 2023, and received {{ facts.petiole.grants }},
        for practical AI applications in agricultural challenges such as pest and disease detection. Petiole Pro is
        {{ facts.petiole.reach }}.
      </p>

      {{ photo(photos.leafMeasurement, sizes="(max-width: 420px) 100vw, 380px", class="page-figure--portrait") }}

      <p>
        I also founded <a class="inline-link" href="{{ facts.links.moomore }}">MooMore</a> ↗, an AI and thermal imaging
        system that detects inflammation in dairy cows before lameness develops. It won the {{ wiw.name }}, announced on
        {{ wiw.announced }}, with a {{ wiw.grant }} grant and a {{ wiw.programme }}. {{ facts.moomore.status }}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <h2>The problem I keep coming back to</h2>

    <div class="bio-card">
      <p>
        A measurement that matters is locked behind specialist equipment, so the people who need it never take it.
      </p>
      <p>
        With Petiole Pro that measurement was leaf area, and the answer was a smartphone camera. With MooMore it is
        inflammation, and the answer is a thermal sensor. The crop and the cow are different; the shape of the problem
        is identical. <a class="inline-link" href="/moomore/">Why I added dairy cattle to my crop AI work</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section" id="recognition">
    <h2>Recognition</h2>

    {# The canonical list. The Person structured data repeats these sentences
       word for word, from the same facts.json entries. #}
    <div class="bio-card">
      <ul class="recognition-list">
        {% for item in facts.recognition %}
        <li>
          <strong>{{ item.title }}</strong> — {{ item.text }}
          {% for link in item.links %}{% set external = link.url.startsWith("http") %}<a class="inline-link" href="{{ link.url }}"{% if external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ link.label }}</a>{{ " ↗" if external else " →" }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
        <li>
          <strong>Petiole Pro</strong>
          <ul>
            {% for item in facts.petiole.recognition %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
            <li>{{ facts.petiole.grantsLine }}</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      {{ photo(photos.womenInInnovationForum, sizes="(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 760px") }}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <h2>Education and professional training</h2>

    <div class="bio-card">
      <ul class="bio-list">
        <li><strong>UPOV Examination of Applications for Plant Breeders’ Rights</strong> — 2024</li>
        <li><strong>UPOV Certification: Introduction to the UPOV System of Plant Variety Protection under the UPOV Convention</strong> — 2024</li>
        <li><strong>IEMA Foundation Certificate in Environmental Management</strong> — 2023</li>
        <li><strong>PhD in Business Law</strong> — Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv, Ukraine, 2015</li>
        <li><strong>LL.M in International Commercial Law</strong> — London Metropolitan University, United Kingdom, 2012; fully funded scholarship</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <h2>Key facts</h2>

    <div class="bio-card">
      <ul class="bio-list">
        <li><strong>Name:</strong> Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko</li>
        <li><strong>Role:</strong> {{ facts.positioning.line }}</li>
        <li><strong>Ventures:</strong> {{ facts.roles | join("; ") }}</li>
        <li><strong>Books:</strong> {% for book in books %}<em>{{ book.fullTitle }}</em>{% if book.series %} ({{ book.series.name }}, book {{ book.series.number }}){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %} — <a href="/books/">see all books</a></li>
        <li><strong>Audience:</strong> LinkedIn, the {{ facts.newsletter.name }}, the {{ facts.live.short }} and YouTube; current figures are on the <a href="/partner/">Partnerships page</a></li>
        <li><strong>Current venture:</strong> MooMore — AI thermal imaging for early dairy lameness detection, <a href="{{ facts.links.moomore }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">moomore.com</a></li>
        <li><strong>Location:</strong> United Kingdom</li>
        <li><strong>Languages:</strong> {{ facts.languages.list | join(", ") }}</li>
        <li><strong>Main field:</strong> AI in agriculture, food quality assurance, entrepreneurship, female leadership</li>
        <li><strong>Award:</strong> {{ wiw.name }} — {{ wiw.status }}</li>
        <li><strong>Award announced:</strong> {{ wiw.announced }}</li>
        <li><strong>Awarded for:</strong> {{ wiw.forLong }}</li>
        <li><strong>Grant value:</strong> {{ wiw.grant }}</li>
        <li><strong>Programme duration:</strong> {{ wiw.programme | capitalize }}</li>
        <li><strong>Selection:</strong> {{ wiw.selection | capitalize }}</li>
        <li><strong>Award profile:</strong> <a href="{{ wiw.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Innovate UK project page</a></li>
        <li><strong>Recognition:</strong> {{ facts.award.topVoice.name }}, {{ facts.award.topVoice.when }}</li>
        <li><strong>Innovate UK:</strong> Women in Innovation Community Forum Member {{ facts.award.wiwForum.cohort }}; {{ facts.petiole.grantsLine }}</li>
        <li><strong>Oxford Farming Conference:</strong> {{ facts.award.ofc.name }}</li>
        <li><strong>WIPO / ITC SheTrades:</strong> Fellow of the IP mentorship programme for young women’s businesses, {{ facts.award.wipo.year }}</li>
        <li><strong>Virgin StartUp:</strong> Step Up Alumna {{ facts.award.virgin.year }}</li>
        <li><strong>Petiole Pro recognition:</strong> {{ facts.petiole.recognition | join(", ") }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <p class="pointer-box">
      Need a bio or a headshot for your programme? → <a class="inline-link" href="/press-kit/">Press &amp; organiser kit</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-section" style="text-align: center;">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/?type=speaking">Book Maryna</a>
  </section>
</section>
